<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> (meta) Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Two variants of the article, one describing the SCP upon discovery and initial tests, the other after learning about it's true scope and it's attempts to escape</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Self aware NPC attempts to break out to the real world, after Foundation tries to contain it, and learns about multi-layered nature of the Foundation reality, created specifically to stop pataphysical threats</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Foundation learns about the existence of a self aware character from roleplaying games, whose name is a cognitohazard, that forces people perceiving it to include this character in their roleplaying activities. They try to contain it, like any other memetically spreading SCP, but it did not want to have its freedom restricted, so it decided to break out to the real world. Foundation, prepared for this kind of pataphysical dangers, created beforehand many layers of fictional realities, each identical to the top one, with Earth, Foundation and all the jazz, to contain entities traveling upwards through layers of fictional realities.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Afaik there are no skips going &quot;upwards'' through the reality layers, besides <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3812">SCP-3812</a>, who accidently went from our reality one level higher, but we don't have any coming from &quot;below&quot; and on purpose. Similarly, there is a multitude of fictional (from the in-universe point of view) SCPs but not much connected to the roleplaying (books and computer games get the majority of attention in this area afaik). I'm also planning on exploring limits of the mentioned cognitohazard, and the entity itself through test logs (something I see rather rarely, but find personally fascinating).</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> English is not my first language (as you can probably tell) and I'll be thankful for pointing any misspellings or grammar mistakes. Also I never before used any &#187;real&#171; internet forum more complicated than facebook or reddit, so I'm sorry in advance for my mistakes while trying to make sense of it (I hope that I created this post in the right way). Thanks for reading, I hope you will like my idea, and maybe I'll manage to get the greenlight for my first SCP ^^</p>
