			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864299">
									

<p>Thank you for your time and feedback, I see now that I didn't explain some things well enough in the original post (and also, I didn't want to go over the word limit) so I'll try to clarify them here</p>
<p>I divided my response into blocks, each block refers to one &quot;chunk&quot; of your post</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Refrain from calling the SCP an “NPC”. It’s not a programmed character, it’s a sentient or semi-sentient non-physical entity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I definetly would not call it that in actuall article, I used term NPC here to better explain what it actually is.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>First, the SCP multiverse wasn’t created by the Foundation to stop certain types of anomalies. The multiverse has many different stories about its origin, but the Foundation never had the power to create a whole multiverse.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Afaik there are two kinds of multiverses in Foundation lore. There is the &quot;horizontal&quot; one, the more traditional kind of multiverse, which I think is the one you think about, with many parrarel worlds. I meant the &quot;vertical&quot; kind, the narrative one, where there are many layers of reality, each is like a fiction to the beeings from the &quot;higher&quot; universes. And if &quot;lower&quot; universes are like fiction to us, we can easily create another world, by simply imaging it up.</p>
<p>It is possible I messed up something in the way the fictional layers of reality work, but from what I know it was already reffered in a few SCPs, including the mentioned <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3812">SCP-3812</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2614">SCP-2614</a> and <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/sandrewswann-s-proposal">Database SCP-001 proposal</a></p>
<p>And here the layers of reality are fictional universes within fictional universes etc. to stop or slow down things that originated somewhere &quot;low&quot; and are somehow resistant to influence from above (because otherwise they would be easily stopped)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And second, I don’t actually think that a self aware RPG character would be able to exist in multiple realities nor have the power to travel between them.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It starts to go up, breaking from the fictional reality to the one higher up. It does not travel between non-fictional parrel universes, nor it exists in more than one. Travelling between fictional worlds if obviously a diffrent thing, since it somehow has to be able to apear in difrent RPGs</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Making your SCP overpowered is kinda cliche and a really easy way of getting downvoted.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yes, I would like to avoid doing another Appolyon or whatever. I understand that its &quot;breaking to the real world&quot; and such seems like its a totally OP thing, but I try my best to 1. make sure it has reasonable limitations 2. there is a way to contain it, that is not overtly complicated and hard to achieve</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Why would his name be a cognitohazard?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would its name be a cognitohazard? I thought about hinting on some relationship with fairies, with the power of True Names and such.</p>
<p>Why would its name be clasified by Foundation as a cognitohazard? Because people after seeing it develop a compulsion to include it in their roleplaying games.</p>
<p>Why I, as an author, would I make its name a cognitohazard? It was th central point of the SCP before I came up with the &quot;going up through layers of reality&quot; stuff, it was &quot;a name of an SCP that forces you to roleplay as it during RPGs&quot; and then I played some more with the idea, I read more about pathaphisical SCPs and decided that it makes sense to connect those two things. It is possible that was a bad idea, but without it this SCP lacked some spark for me :v</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And if he is a rpg character, how would the Foundation know that he is sentient? If you’re taking about paper and pencil rpg, then it’s basically impossible for a character to be sentient, since the person using that character would choose everything they would do.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's part of reason why it is anomalous, the person roleplaying as it may seem like its just roleplaying, and it might be indistinguishable most of time, but in some cases (as in some immersion-heavy LARPs) people would do things that will make sense for the character but would not for them to the extreme degree, for example the plot is that the characters are locked in during a blizzard without a food, so the person under the influence of the SCP straight up kills other player, because of fictional reasons. The characters wants and needs &quot;override&quot; the wants and needs of the person roleplaying. That's how the foundation can say that there is something weird going on, and after Foundation's interrogation of this SCP using RPG games they can learn that it is a separate entity from the &quot;host&quot; the person roleplaying as it, and not just a weird effect caused by the SCPs name (altough its a posible reinterpretation, and if this idea will not get greenlighted and will need to be reworked, it might be the path I'll follow).</p>
<p>And yes, I thought about it as a paper and pencil RPG like D&amp;D, rather than computer games like Skyrim and such.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, just because a certain character is played multiple times by multiple people doesn’t mean it’s an anomaly, it could mean that a certain character is really famous and people like using him in their roleplaying activities.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's how it at first evades detection by the Foundation. But in the combination of the cognitohazard caused by its name, people are mentally forced to play as him. Free will and diference with &quot;what if people just want to do that&quot; gets imo tricky when talking about memetic influences.</p>
<p>It's kinda like a diference between, for example, a song that is just very cool and lot of people like it, and a song that forces you to dance to it, even if you wouldn't want to.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Like I said before, the Foundation isn’t able to build multiple realities, and if they could send entities through these layers, then it would be a infinite loop of the same entity traveling each time to other layers, including our own. The reason why is that, since there are infinite realities, then there is one “below” us with that same entity, and it would eventually reach us again. That’s probably the worst way of containing an SCP, since they would always come back.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think that I don't fully understand your explanation with the looping realities. I think you may have ment that creation of the copy of Foundation world also copies the entity, but then, given the fact that created universe is moldable like a fiction (except for this SCP and others that are resistant to those changes), a personn creating the copy can just leave out the SCP. It kinda works like elongating the stairs, by adding new steps at the end, and moving previous ones dawnwards, which is not perfect, but allows the Foundation to find other way to stop something that comes to us from fictional realities.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>If you’re going to explore that, you need to describe everything here. That means you need to describe all the effects it causes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was limited by the word constraint, and also thought that a greenlight request is supposed to be a qucik summary of what do we wan't to do. I obviously want to include those logs in the article.</p>
<p>I don't know if you want me to write them now, but in case you do, here is some I have thought about, related to the cognitohazardous name (it's obviously a work in progress so it's not all that i think will be there, and what I already thought about might change):</p>
<ol>
<li>the information is importnat, not the way it's relied. Doesn't matter, if it's read in any alphabet, spoken, or somebody decrypts it in their head, it still will wokr</li>
<li>random string of letters don't work. The name must be created or shown with the awarness that it's a name. If you see for example part of a serial number that is identical to the name of the SCP, it won't work</li>
<li>it only catches on humans so far, monkey that was taught sign language wasn't influenced by it</li>
<li>People exposed to the name, that had no previous contanct with roleplaying create some form of it on their own</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>It’s not that interesting to me. I feel this is some kind of bad mix of SCP-3812, SCP-079 and Monika from DDLC. The idea of using other realities is also flawed, since most of it doesn’t make sense. Also, I don’t think an entity that lives inside a roleplaying game could do much, since I believe he would be bound by the laws of that game. So basically, no matter if it’s a paper and pencil rpg or a computer game, it would never be able to leave its realm. I recommend you to remodel the concept and try different things, because I don’t think it would be greenlighted as it is. Good luck! ;)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I understand the connection to <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3812">SCP-3812</a> (I made this connection in the orginial post myself) since they work on similar principle of ascesion from fiction to reality, and my idea is a kind of difrent take on it. I kind of see the conection with<br />
SCP-079, with beeing angry about imprisonment (altough I thought it is a kind of common emotion among self aware SCPs contained by Foundation. I would be a bit unhappy myself if I were contained. I didn't play DDLC so can't respond to that.</p>
<p>I understand that it might be not the most interesting, mayby my explanations will make it a bit more appealing. Your feedback made me think about changing some parts of this SCP, eg. going back to original idea, without the ascesion and stuff, and just have a wacky memetic thing that forces poeple to roleplay as certain character, or mayby limit the ascesion, for example that the SCP breaks out to real world, see it's kinda trash, and want's to go back. I would be thankfull for your opinion on those alternatives.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I would like to thank you again for the time to write the feedback and read my response. I think some of my responses may seem a bit passive-aggresive, it was not my intention, any feedback is very important to me, because then I can correct what I did wrongly and do better next time, so I really apreciate the time you took to look into my idea ^^</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

