<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Regarding the vertical layers of reality</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What you said is true and I did understand it wrong. I apologize for that. Still, why would the Foundation keep making that entity travel between other stories/realities? The reason why I'm asking this is because, as far as I've seen, this entity doesn't have the power to go into the real world, regardless of the story he's in. So it basically poses no threat at all, as long as people doesn't know his name and nobody plays as him. If the Foundation makes him go to another reality, like a story book, his name would be there, and now The Foundation would need to contain everything regarding that book. There are two options to contain this SCP: 1. Destroy everything regarding him and leave at least one thing about him inside one of the Foundation sites. Testing would always end up with amnestics, so it should be okay; 2. The Foundation creates a new story, either written, drawn or anything else, and make the entity go there. I believe option number 1 would be way easier and the most logical solution, since it's something pratical. The Foundation tries to make everything as simple as possible.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the person roleplaying as it may seem like its just roleplaying, and it might be indistinguishable most of time</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So the entity is able to have a little bit of control over the player?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Regarding him wanting to break into the real world</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How exactly would it do that? Even if it's able to control the player, all it can do is make the player do things inside the RPG, and not outside. Since you didn't describe any powers or abilities besides the cognitohazard thing and the partial mind control, this SCP won't be able to leave their reality as it is now.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I don't know if you want me to write them now</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What would be best is that you describe its abilities as a brief summary as well. The problem about abilities is that it might change the view a critter has about it. We need to know what it is and what it can do. You also need to briefly describe the SCP characteristics and personality. Since you're worried about word limit, you could just delete unimportant bits, like long examples or similar things.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>here is some I have thought about, related to the cognitohazardous name</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not talking about its name, what I meant was what he can actually do besides that. If the cognitohazardous name is the only ability he has, then this SCP isn't much different from others, and as a result, it's unoriginal.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>going back to original idea, without the ascesion and stuff, and just have a wacky memetic thing that forces poeple to roleplay as certain character</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That would be a generic SCP idea, so this alone wouldn't be enough to get approved. It is a good starting point, though.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>mayby limit the ascesion, for example that the SCP breaks out to real world, see it's kinda trash, and want's to go back.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And now we go to those questions: What does the SCP really want? Why does it want to go to the real world? What exactly made him think that the real world &quot;sucks&quot;? And why would he want to go back?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

